// spec: LEX-023, LEX-029
//
// '''' is the Char holding a quote: one character of value, however many of
// source.  The doubling is NOTATION for a character, and notation must not
// change a type.
//
// ⚠️ This was measured on the source SPAN, which made the same character carry
// two types depending on how it was spelled -- so a quote was not equal to
// itself, and had an ordinal under one spelling only.

WriteLn ('''' is Char);
WriteLn (#39 is Char);
WriteLn ('''' = #39);
WriteLn (Ord (''''));

// '' is the empty String, and there is no empty Char [LEX-029].
WriteLn ('' is String);
WriteLn (Length (''));
